<title>GERMANY: Rheinmetall 1996 profit rises sharply.</title>
<headline>Rheinmetall 1996 profit rises sharply.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German electronics and engineering group Rheinmetall AG said on Wednesday that group net profit surged to 45.4 million marks in 1996 from 2.6 million marks the year before.</p>
<p>Group sales rose 10.2 percent to 3.655 billion marks and incoming orders hit a record 4.46 billion marks, up 23 percent. The company said it would pay unchanged dividends of seven marks per ordinary share and eight marks per preference share.  </p>
<p>The company said in a regulatory statement that it aimed to nearly double sales to around seven billion marks this year and to achieve pre-tax earnings of almost 100 million marks.</p>
<p>The company's 1997 results would be marked by the acquisitions of the Hirschmann group, STN Atlas Elektronik and Kolbenschmidt.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097 150</p>
